# packages-node-host.list — the host packages a cluster NODE needs beyond
# packages-k8s.list, for a board whose own base list is a desktop's.
#
# The Raspberry Pi carries every one of these in its BASE packages.list (beside its
# Pi-only firmware/EEPROM/kernel atoms), so a Pi node build never reads this file.
# The Orange Pi node roles (build-orangepi5-stage4.sh, build-orangepi4-lts-stage4.sh;
# EXPERIMENTAL, hardware validation pending) start from the Orange Pi desktop base
# list, which lacks them, and append this list after packages-k8s.list.
# tests/scripts/test-role-key-spelling.sh section E asserts the Orange Pi node set
# covers the Pi base list minus its Raspberry Pi hardware atoms, so an atom added to
# the Pi base list and missing here fails that test.

# Host firewall: hugmesh-firewall-reconcile loads its release-state rules with nft.
# Without nft no rules ever load; the reconcile then marks the node UNPROTECTED
# (/run/hugmesh/firewall-health/) and exits 1, so its boot oneshot shows red.
net-firewall/nftables
net-firewall/conntrack-tools

# Pod networking tools kube-proxy / the CNI plugins / kubeadm preflight call.
sys-apps/iproute2
sys-apps/ethtool

# Encrypted data disks + LVM (the node storage bake, --encrypt-root).
sys-fs/cryptsetup
sys-fs/lvm2
sys-apps/nvme-cli

# SELinux policy for containers and VMs, and the policy query tools.
sec-policy/selinux-container
sec-policy/selinux-virt
app-admin/setools
